Z||000004||BENGAL4||06-13-2001||04:25 AM||||Hey guys. I am alive and kicking.<P>Cheever - I won't be coming to Houston until September or October. My customer has to go to Peru for awhile, so we had to postphone the trip. When I do go, I will get a hold of you so we can have a few adult beverages and talk Fiero's. BTW the other e-mail is bwilburn4@yahoo.com.<P>Phil - My car is finished. I thought I was going to Toronto this week, but with my girls softball going on, I can't get up there until the weekend after the 4th of July. I spoke to the Fiero Shop and they said it is running great. The OBDI computer and the custom chip has eliminated the rev and speed limiters. Joe said he reved it up to 6200 rpm, and it did not shut down. He said it is the fastest, 3800 S/C, that he has ever driven. Well I guess we will see.<P>Scott - Been meaning to call this week. I had surgery on my left wrist and hand last week for carpal tunnel. Well it worked, the pain is gone. I'll call you today sometime.<P>Dave - My favorite ape. I guess, under different circumstances, I should raise some hell with someone. With the family issues over the last year, the Fiero was on the back burner. This spring I started pushing them to finish and it was one bug after the other. The computer wouldn't work and so on and so on. I hope things are better with you. Stay away from Bambi,OK.  ||||reg||10
